  "_comment": [
    "Five coaches' walk-in paper forms, filled in, for the lifecycle check's walk-in step",
    "(Server/scripts/seedWalkIn.js). The JPEGs beside this file are RENDERED from it:",
    "",
    "  npm --prefix Server run walkin:fixtures",
    "",
    "which prints the real form (src/services/walk-in/form-pdf.service.js), writes these",
    "values into its boxes in a printed hand -- one digit per date box, names in capitals,",
    "a tick in each apparatus box -- rasterises it and tilts it slightly, the way a phone",
    "on a desk photographs a page. Re-run it after any change to the form's geometry",
    "(FORM_VERSION); the step refuses images whose version differs from the form's.",
    "",
    "Everyone here is invented: no real child, coach or phone number. The coaches and",
    "teams are the desk's own, created by the step; they are on no roster. Each desk",
    "enters a different meet at a different level, so five meets get one more team, and",
    "every child's name and birthday is unique, so the desk's one-child-one-Player-ID",
    "check registers each of them rather than offering an existing account.",
    "",
    "`rows` is what the OCR must read back, field for field. The step asserts it before",
    "anything is registered, so a misread fails the run instead of seeding a misspelt child."
  ],
